dataset: fixed topology (density=1.0, same graph as every other
experiment) + ONE shared x0 (drawn once) -- x0-ANCHORED perturbation:
each node's box is rebuilt AROUND x0 by rescaling the base market's
own distance from x0 to each edge (D_min/D_max, G_min/G_max) by two
INDEPENDENT positive factors in [0.5,2.0] -- x0 is mathematically
inside the box for every draw, by construction, no clip ever needed.
D*/G_res keep their own independent 'level' factor +/-20%.
Infeasible or negative draws discarded+resampled.
